Note: =====================================================================
Note: test_notation_to_musicxml_example.flow — Phase 39 regression test
Note: =====================================================================
Note:
Note: Composer-facing regression for the writeMusicXML builtin (XML-01).
Note: The deep file-format assertions (XML well-formedness, multi-part shape,
Note: D-39-07 slur grouping, two-run cmp-clean determinism) are owned by
Note: MusicXmlExportTests.cs. This .flow test gates the "composer-facing
Note: call doesn't crash" surface via the Phase 35 (test "name" lazy(body))
Note: framework.

use "@test"
use "@notation-io"
use "@std"

Note: Top-level setup — build the Song and call writeMusicXML at script
Note: registration time. The (test ...) call only deferred-asserts an
Note: invariant that holds AFTER the call returned. This mirrors the
Note: pattern in tests/test_parameterized_example.flow.

tempo 120 {
    timesig 4/4 {
        key Cmajor {
            section testIntro {
                Sequence piano = | C4q D4q E4q F4q |
            }
            Song song = [testIntro]
            (writeMusicXML "/tmp/flow_test_to_musicxml.musicxml" song)
        }
    }
}

(test "writeMusicXML executed without error" lazy((assert true)))
